# Syntara Combined Monorepo — Code Owners
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# Scope policy:
#   - Areas are owned by the team that maintains them.
#   - The default rule lists both product teams, so routine repo hygiene
#     (.gitignore, README, Makefile, .env.example, .claude/, .mcp.json,
#     PR template) can be approved by any backend or UI engineer rather than
#     blocking on leads.
#   - @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads is reserved for governance and
#     architecture: this file, the licences, the standards and decision
#     records that bind every domain, and the framework layer both stacks
#     build on. Routine, feature-driven churn inside those trees is handed
#     back to the owning team on an explicit later rule.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Safety net so no path is ever unowned, including new top-level files and
# directories. Approval from EITHER team satisfies it.
* @syntara-orchestration/syntara-backend @syntara-orchestration/ui-team

# ── Backend (Python/FastAPI) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/backend/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-backend

# ── Frontend (React/TypeScript) ──────────────────────────────────────────
/frontend/ @syntara-orchestration/ui-team

# UX design system — requires UX team review.
# The skill moved to the repo root when the monorepo was consolidated; the old
# rule still pointed at /frontend/.claude/skills/patternfly-ux-design-system.md,
# which no longer exists, so uxd-team had silently lost ownership of it.
/.claude/skills/frontend-patternfly-ux/ @syntara-orchestration/uxd-team
/frontend/.cursor/rules/patternfly-ux-design-system.mdc @syntara-orchestration/uxd-team

# ── CI/CD — workflows, custom actions, and CI-adjacent config ────────────
/.github/scripts/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-ci-stability
/.github/workflows/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-ci-stability
/.github/actions/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-ci-stability
/.github/actionlint.yaml @syntara-orchestration/syntara-ci-stability
/.github/dependabot.yml @syntara-orchestration/syntara-ci-stability

# ── Release / packaging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.tekton/ @syntara-orchestration/release-team
/backend/containers/ @syntara-orchestration/release-team
# The previous rule here was "./frontend/packages/syntara-ui/" — a leading "./"
# is invalid CODEOWNERS syntax, so it never matched anything. Narrowed to the
# shipping artifacts on purpose: pointing it at the whole directory would make
# @release-team the sole owner of the UI app and displace @ui-team.
/frontend/packages/syntara-ui/Containerfile @syntara-orchestration/release-team
/frontend/packages/syntara-ui/Containerfile.konflux @syntara-orchestration/release-team
/frontend/packages/syntara-ui/nginx.conf.template @syntara-orchestration/release-team

# ── Governance & architecture — @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads ────────────
# Deliberately narrow. Everything below is either a decision that binds the
# whole system or the framework layer every feature is built on.
# KEEP THIS SECTION LAST — it must override the area rules above.

# Repository governance
/.github/CODEOWNERS @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/.github/AI_AGENT_POLICY.md @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/GOVERNANCE.md @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/LICENSE @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/backend/LICENSE @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/frontend/packages/syntara-ui/LICENSE @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads

# Architecture decision records and engineering standards
/backend/decision-records.md @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
/backend/docs/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads

# Backend framework layer — the substrate every domain package builds on
# (router discovery, models, auth, logging, websocket, workers, error handling)
/backend/src/syntara/core/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
# ...but routine, feature-driven churn inside it stays with the backend team.
# These two account for ~57% of all core/ changes and are almost never
# architectural: one Alembic revision per feature, one setting per feature.
/backend/src/syntara/core/config/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-backend
/backend/src/syntara/core/database/migrations/versions/ @syntara-orchestration/syntara-backend

# Frontend framework — only the API client bootstrap needs leads review.
/frontend/packages/syntara-ui/src/client.tsx @syntara-orchestration/syntara-leads
